{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, after all parameter priors have been declared. Other data variables are used only as context inputs for deterministic predictor construction.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix

  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y; // Variates
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n,] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;      // Intercept
  vector[M] beta;  // Linear slopes
}

model {
  // Prior model
  alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta ~ normal(0, 1);

  // Vectorized observation model
  y ~ bernoulli_logit(alpha + deltaX * beta);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  vector[N] logit_p = alpha + deltaX * beta;
  array[N] int y_pred = bernoulli_logit_rng(logit_p);
}
